---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + "/";
---
<Layout title="Gen Rise Media — Rahul Jain">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href={base + "origins/"}>&larr; Origins</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Gen Rise Media</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Managing Editor &middot; Oct 2017 &ndash; Dec 2020</p>
    <section>
      <p class="blurb">
        What became Gen Rise Media started as something I built with a friend and fellow student. Freshman
        year of high school, after running unsuccessfully for class office on small,
        practical platforms — eco-friendly lunch trays, faster evacuation routes — I realized the actual
        problem was bigger: students wanted to write and talk publicly about the issues that mattered to
        them (environmentalism, racism, mental health, pop culture) and had no outlet to do it. So the two
        of us built one — an <strong>online magazine called Lune</strong> — which within months had writers publishing
        from around the country. It went through two more rebrands, to Opal and then to Gen Rise Media, as
        it grew, and I stayed on as <strong>Managing Editor from Oct 2017 to Dec 2020</strong>: writing and enforcing
        our style guides, recruiting and selecting new staff, and managing the finances for our print
        issues.
      </p>
      <p class="blurb">
        The growth mattered more to me than the title. Through partnership-building, SEO, and a
        restructuring of how the editorial and outreach teams worked together, we grew from a small
        volunteer group into an organization of <strong>80+ staff</strong>, with over <strong>100,000 all-time site views</strong>
        and <strong>10,000+ Instagram followers</strong>. Gen Rise Media has since wound down, but it was my first real
        experience scaling something — building the systems and structure that let a volunteer organization
        keep working reliably as more people joined, which is a version of the same problem I get paid to
        solve now.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
